1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,190
Hi, you must be Daniel. Thanks for coming in today.

2
00:00:06,490 --> 00:00:09,561
Thank you for having me. It's nice to meet you.

3
00:00:09,861 --> 00:00:12,529
Nice to meet you too. Please, have a seat.

4
00:00:12,529 --> 00:00:15,030
So, could you tell me a little bit about yourself?

5
00:00:15,330 --> 00:00:23,028
Sure. I just graduated with a degree in logistics, and I've been working part-time at a shipping company for about a year.

6
00:00:23,328 --> 00:00:25,855
That sounds interesting. What did you do there?

7
00:00:26,155 --> 00:00:30,393
I was in charge of tracking shipments and updating our customers.

8
00:00:30,393 --> 00:00:33,423
It taught me how to stay calm when things go wrong.

9
00:00:33,723 --> 00:00:35,701
Good. Why do you want to work with us?

10
00:00:36,001 --> 00:00:43,485
To be honest, I've always wanted to work on a global team, and I think my experience is a good fit for this role.

11
00:00:43,785 --> 00:00:45,808
What would you say is your biggest strength?

12
00:00:46,108 --> 00:00:52,287
I'd say I'm a fast learner. When I don't know something, I ask questions and figure it out quickly.

13
00:00:52,587 --> 00:00:54,110
And what about a weakness?

14
00:00:54,410 --> 00:01:00,538
Well, I used to take on too much at once. Now I make a list and focus on what matters most.

15
00:01:00,838 --> 00:01:03,733
That makes sense. Do you have any questions for me?

16
00:01:04,033 --> 00:01:08,880
Yes, actually. What does a typical day look like for someone in this position?

17
00:01:09,180 --> 00:01:15,336
Good question. You'd be working closely with our operations team, so we're gonna have a lot of meetings at first.

18
00:01:15,636 --> 00:01:18,623
That sounds great. I'm looking forward to it.

19
00:01:18,923 --> 00:01:21,653
Great. We'll get back to you by the end of the week.

20
00:01:21,953 --> 00:01:24,040
Thank you so much for your time.

21
00:01:26,590 --> 00:01:30,460
Okay, let's get started. Leo, can you give us a quick update?

22
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:36,378
Sure. The new tracking system is almost ready, but we're running a little behind schedule.

23
00:01:36,678 --> 00:01:38,410
How far behind are we?

24
00:01:38,710 --> 00:01:43,748
About two days. We found a problem with the data, and we're still working on it.

25
00:01:44,048 --> 00:01:46,105
I see. Daniel, what do you think?

26
00:01:46,405 --> 00:01:51,654
I think we could ask the IT team for help. They fixed something similar last month.

27
00:01:51,954 --> 00:01:54,527
That's a good point. I didn't know that.

28
00:01:54,827 --> 00:01:57,341
Let's do that. Can you set up a call with them?

29
00:01:57,641 --> 00:02:00,626
Sure. Let me check their schedule and get back to you.

30
00:02:00,926 --> 00:02:03,989
One more thing. Could you send me the report by Friday?

31
00:02:04,289 --> 00:02:07,186
Sorry, did you say Friday or Thursday?

32
00:02:07,486 --> 00:02:10,304
Friday is fine. Does that work for everyone?

33
00:02:10,604 --> 00:02:11,806
Works for me.

34
00:02:12,106 --> 00:02:14,766
Great. That's all for today. Thanks, everyone.

